linux-rockchip64-ysp-alpha-7.3-rc2 (7.3.0~rc2+rk3588rewritealpha20260913-0ubuntu1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Re-layer the rewrite composite onto official v7.3-rc2 (df2908090cda3).
    The Armbian rockchip64-bleedingedge patch layer was regenerated for 7.3
    from build checkout 2a53f158 (`./compile.sh kernel-patches-to-git
    BOARD=rock-5b BRANCH=bleedingedge KERNELBRANCH=tag:v7.3-rc2`), producing
    snapshot commit f57f0d57308eb; the 370-commit rewrite series then replayed
    onto it without a single conflict.
  * The rewrite payload is byte-identical to rk3588-rewrite-mainline at
    12a6a61b76aca, itself the maintained mainline tip rebased from v7.2-rc6
    to v7.3-rc2. That rebase needed one resolution, in rockchip-iommu.c:
    upstream 414cb6f3ac621 dropped the global rk_ops in favour of per-device
    ops, so the port keeps upstream's removal and retains only the rewrite's
    forward declaration of rk_iommu_ops.
  * Supersedes the never-uploaded 7.2-rc5 alpha definition. New source and
    binary package names in the ysp-alpha-7.3-rc2-rockchip64 slot,
    co-installable beside every other kernel slot.
  * No boot, hardware, or KUnit runtime evidence exists for this composite.

